# Material Response Analysis and ANFIS-Based Thermal Diffusivity Estimation

## Overview
This project investigates the responses of eight materials subjected to temporal excitations. It combines exploratory data analysis, statistical analysis, feature extraction, and intelligent modeling to estimate material thermal diffusivity.

## Part 1 — Exploratory Data Analysis
- Analysis of time-dependent material responses.
- Automatic detection of excitation events.
- Extraction of response duration, maximum, minimum, and average slope.
- Statistical analysis of the influence of excitation duration.
- 3D visualization and comparison of material responses.

## Part 2 — ANFIS Modeling
- Thermal diffusivity estimation using an Adaptive Neuro-Fuzzy Inference System (ANFIS).
- Data normalization and feature selection.
- Model training and validation using different data-splitting strategies.
- Comparison of two input configurations:
  - Duration and maximum response.
  - Duration and average slope.
- Analysis of estimation errors and generalization limitations.

## Tools
- MATLAB
- Excel
- ANFIS modeling (`genfis`, `anfis`, `evalfis`)

## Key Findings
- Excitation duration strongly influences response amplitude and average slope.
- Different materials exhibit distinct response characteristics.
- The ANFIS model captures the general trends in thermal diffusivity, although estimation accuracy varies depending on the input features and validation strategy.

